# verify-build — canonical build / install / verify recipe (per frontend)

> The 5-step verify gate from `skills/dev/assign/SKILL.md §5`, with stack-specific commands. Devs cite this file in handoffs.

## The 5-step gate

Every task-md execution finishes with these 5 steps **before commit**. Skip any → §5 fail → handoff `-block.md` (not `-result.md`).

| # | Step | Pass criteria |
|:-:|---|---|
| 1 | **Build** | exit 0; zero error; warnings reviewed (escalate new warnings) |
| 2 | **Install** | exit 0; app launches on the connected device |
| 3 | **Launch + Log** | manually exercise the changed code path; runtime log has no new crash / fatal / `*: E` error |
| 4 | **Screenshot** | capture UI; diff vs design-truth or task-md `-before` snapshot |
| 5 | **Lint** | exit 0 (or only pre-existing warnings unchanged) |

Optional 6th step for perf tasks: **Profile** (see `perf-diagnosis.md`).

## Stack-specific commands

Values come from `.sulde-config.yaml: build_verify[<stack>]`. Defaults reproduced here for reference.

### Android (`mobile-android`)

```bash
./gradlew :app:assembleDebug                              # build
# Windows: gradlew.bat :app:assembleDebug

adb install -r app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk  # install
adb shell am start -n {package}/.MainActivity             # launch
adb logcat -d AndroidRuntime:E '*:S' > log.txt            # log
adb shell screencap -p > after.png                        # screenshot
./gradlew lint                                            # lint
```

### iOS (`mobile-ios`)

```bash
xcodebuild -project {project}.xcodeproj \
           -scheme {scheme} \
           -destination 'platform=iOS,id={udid}' \
           build                                          # build (macOS only)

# install — choose one:
ios-deploy --id {udid} --bundle {app_path} --justlaunch
xcrun devicectl device install app --device {udid} {app_path}

xcrun devicectl process launch --device {udid} {bundle_id}  # launch
idevicesyslog -u {udid} > log.txt                           # log
xcrun simctl io booted screenshot after.png                 # screenshot (simulator)
xcrun devicectl device snapshot --device {udid}             # screenshot (real device)
swiftlint                                                   # lint
```

### Flutter (`mobile-flutter`)

```bash
flutter build apk --debug         # build
flutter install                   # install
flutter run --release             # launch
flutter logs > log.txt            # log
flutter screenshot --out after.png  # screenshot
flutter analyze                   # lint
```

### Harmony (`mobile-harmony`)

```bash
./hvigorw assembleHap --mode debug                          # build
# Windows: hvigorw.bat assembleHap --mode debug

hdc install -r build/default/outputs/default/{hap}.hap      # install
hdc shell aa start -a {ability} -b {bundle}                 # launch
hdc shell hilog | grep {bundle} > log.txt                   # log
hdc shell snapshot_display -f /data/local/tmp/screen.png \
  && hdc file recv /data/local/tmp/screen.png after.png     # screenshot
./hvigorw lint                                              # lint
```

## What gets stored where

Each step's output goes to `<frontend>/.ai-workspace/`:

| Step | Path | Naming |
|---|---|---|
| Build | (in handoff inline; no file) | quote BUILD SUCCESSFUL line + duration |
| Install | (inline) | `adb install` / `hdc install` exit + Success line |
| Log | `.ai-workspace/diag/{date}-{task}-log.txt` | full file referenced from handoff |
| Screenshot | `.ai-workspace/screenshots/{date}-{task}-after.png` | + matching `-before.png` if visual change |
| Lint | (inline if green; file if warnings to escalate) | `.ai-workspace/diag/{date}-{task}-lint.txt` |

## When verify is allowed to be partial

| Scenario | Verify partial? |
|---|---|
| Pure doc / .ai-workspace edits | ✅ skip all 5; note "no code change" in handoff |
| Config-only change (no UI / no runtime path) | ✅ steps 1+5 only |
| Test-only change | ✅ steps 1+5+ test run output |
| UI / behavioural change | ❌ all 5 mandatory |
| Perf change | ❌ all 5 + profile capture (perf-diagnosis.md) |

## CI vs local

Local verify is the dev's responsibility. CI is the coordinator's safety net. The handoff's `§ verify` section quotes local results; the coordinator runs CI before merging to integration.

When local hardware is unavailable (iOS on Linux/Windows; Harmony device unavailable):

- Push to a CI-only branch
- Reference CI run URL from the handoff
- The §5 verify still must include the CI summary, not just "CI passes"
